# Firework AI — Complete Authentication, Onboarding & Professional Profile System

## 1. Project Context and Critical Instructions

You are working on my existing application, **Firework AI**, previously known as FreelanceLens AI.

Do not create a new application, rebuild the entire project, replace the existing architecture, or remove current features.

Your task is to upgrade the existing application by implementing a complete, functional authentication system, a professional onboarding experience, and a persistent user profile that contains the information needed to personalize AI-powered freelance project analysis.

The current problem is that when I open the application, it immediately displays the application dashboard and appears to treat me as an already registered user, even though I have not entered my professional background, specialization, skills, education, certificates, or experience.

This behavior must be corrected.

**The application must distinguish between an unauthenticated visitor, a newly registered user, and a returning authenticated user.**

Before making changes, inspect the existing authentication logic, routing, database configuration, Firebase integration if present, user state, dashboard, and profile components. Reuse the existing infrastructure whenever possible.

Do not assume Firebase Authentication or Firestore is correctly configured just because they were previously enabled. Verify the current implementation.

